From: b70-notes <b70-notes@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:31:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SYCL Inkling fusions: relative-position FA mask, conv
 state store, router logits; parallel mix/control/relmask kernels

- relmask: the per-head FA mask (PAD MUL_MAT SUB CONT GET_ROWS CONT CPY ADD CPY) as 2 kernels, reads the unpadded bias
- convstore: CONCAT(past, x) + the state CPY as one kernel
- router: the f32 logits mat-vec folded in (4 sub-groups per expert)
- mix: 2 kernels (per-row reductions, then output chunks), was one work-group per token (26.7 -> 12.4 us)
- control: the down projection split into quarters (14.7 -> 12.1 us); <= 8 tokens only (prompt GEMMs are faster)
- span check counts self-references (ggml_cast CPY src[1] == itself); exact alias allowed for single-query mix
- inkling2.cpp: no ggml_cont of row views that are already contiguous (single-token decode), SWA reuses input 0
- profiling: GGML_SYCL_OPPROF=2 + GGML_SYCL_QUEUE_PROFILING=1 gives GPU barrier timestamps per node; fusion names
Decode 2247 launches; NVFP4-Q8_0 tg64 56.7 -> 59.6, pp512 646 -> 752 (FA on).

